# Forum threads list/show implementation evidence

Scope: selected-session thread listing and selected-thread detail only. The endpoint/path and projection follow the sanitized live samples in `forum-schema-paths-live-evidence.json` and the request builder in `spikes/001-auth/examples/forum_schema.rs`. No credential material is included here. This implementation has only fixture validation; it has not made a live request.

## Acceptance trace

| Requirement | Implementation | Fixture evidence | Result / limit |
|---|---|---|---|
| A. CLI both binaries, argument validation before credential load, common JSON/exit mapping | `src/cli.rs` `ForumsAction`; `emit_forum` delegates to `courses_output` | `forums_cli_help_missing_and_unsafe_ids_precede_credentials_for_both_binaries`; list/show pipeline tests assert shared serializer status and exit values | Covered. Missing/unsafe usage behavior tested for both executable names. |
| B. Fixed selected-session POST pages, 20/page, declared total, exact `threadId`, dedupe, prior-page retention | `src/forums.rs` `make_request`, `list_inner`, `row` | `list_pipeline_follows_pages_and_uses_verified_route_body_and_headers`; `empty_is_complete_first_failure_errors_and_duplicates_are_exact`; `malformed_later_list_row_discards_only_that_page`; `later_page_failure_retains_validated_rows_and_reports_partial`; `operation_deadline_spans_pages_and_retains_page_one` | Covered by local HTTP fixtures. Fixture verifies route/body, auth role header inheritance, and no Cookie. |
| C. Context-checked GET, safe detail projection, HTML to text, URL/attachment secrecy | `show_inner`, `visible_text` | `show_pipeline_projects_html_and_attachment_without_fetching_embedded_urls`; `wrong_detail_context_is_rejected_and_malformed_attachment_is_atomic`; `html_text_skips_markup_and_redacts_signed_urls` | Covered with HTML/script/link/image/attachment honeypots. It asserts one request only and no URL output. HTML parsing uses html5ever's documented `parse_document` API ([docs](https://docs.rs/html5ever/latest/html5ever/driver/fn.parse_document.html)). |
| D. Fixed origin, inherited headers, redirect refusal, deadlines, streamed cap, sanitized transport errors | `make_request`, `request_json` | `list_pipeline_follows_pages_and_uses_verified_route_body_and_headers`; `redirect_is_refused_without_forwarding_authorization`; `response_cap_applies_to_chunked_unknown_length_body`; `request_deadline_covers_headers_and_all_response_chunks`; `operation_deadline_spans_pages_and_retains_page_one` | Limits exercised through cfg(test) loopback seam using short durations and a 64-byte cap. Production constants remain 20s request, 60s operation, 8MiB response. |
| E. Pipeline tests and existing checks | Tests in `src/forums.rs` and `tests/cli.rs` | `cargo test --all-targets -- --test-threads=1` passes (82 lib tests, 11 integration tests, all example test targets). A default parallel `cargo test --all-targets` run hit the existing Courses 220ms timing assertion once; that test passed isolated and in the serial full suite. `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, and `cargo build --release` pass. | All commands pass. |

## Explicit limits

- No live API/authenticated verification was performed in this environment. Fixtures do not establish production availability or real credential behavior.
- The current test set does not individually exercise 401, 403, 5xx, closed-port, and malformed-JSON categorization in the forum module. The implementation maps 401/403 to `authorization_required`, non-2xx statuses to `upstream_error`, and transport/timeout/JSON/schema failures to static codes, but those category branches need more direct fixture cases.
- The chunked-cap fixture uses a small test cap to exercise cumulative streaming behavior; it does not transmit a full 8MiB payload.
- No test asserts behavior for every possible upstream pagination metadata spelling. Known continuation signals are detected and fail closed.
- There is no network call for attachment URLs, image URLs, or HTML link targets; fixture assertions verify only the thread list/detail request is observed.

