# Forum threads list/show implementation evidence

Scope: selected-session thread listing and selected-thread detail only. Endpoint and projection notes were derived from sanitized samples recorded in "'`forum-schema-paths-live-evidence.json` and the request builder in `spikes/001-auth/examples/forum_schema.rs`. This implementation has fixture validation; this test batch made no live request.

## Acceptance trace

| Requirement | Implementation | Fixture evidence | Result / limit |
|---|---|---|---|
| A. CLI both binaries, argument validation before credential load, common JSON/exit mapping | `src/cli.rs` `ForumsAction`; `emit_forum` delegates to `courses_output` | `forums_cli_help_missing_and_unsafe_ids_precede_credentials_for_both_binaries`; list/show serializer tests | Covered. Missing/unsafe usage behavior tested for both executable names. |
| B. Fixed selected-session POST pages, 20/page, declared total, exact `threadId`, dedupe, prior-page retention | `src/forums.rs` `make_request`, `list_inner`, `row` | `list_pipeline_follows_pages_and_uses_verified_route_body_and_headers`; `empty_is_complete_first_failure_errors_and_duplicates_are_exact`; `malformed_later_list_row_discards_only_that_page`; `later_page_failure_retains_validated_rows_and_reports_partial`; `operation_deadline_spans_pages_and_retains_page_one` | Local HTTP fixtures verify method/path, complete JSON body, exact synthetic Bearer and five role-header values, no Cookie, and distinct source `id` versus retained `threadId`. Empty, complete, partial, and error mapping are covered. |
| C. Context-checked GET, safe detail projection, HTML to text, URL/attachment secrecy | `show_inner`, `visible_text` | `show_pipeline_projects_html_and_attachment_without_fetching_embedded_urls`; `wrong_detail_context_is_rejected_and_malformed_attachment_is_atomic`; `html_text_skips_markup_and_redacts_signed_urls` | The detail fixture points HTML link/image/attachment URLs to a bounded local listening observer that stays active during SHOW; it observes zero requests. Main thread fixture observes one GET. The serializer omits attachment URLs. HTML parsing uses html5ever'"'s documented "'`parse_document` API ([docs](https://docs.rs/html5ever/latest/html5ever/driver/fn.parse_document.html)). |
| D. Fixed origin, inherited headers, redirect refusal, deadlines, streamed cap, sanitized transport errors | `make_request`, `request_json` | `list_pipeline_follows_pages_and_uses_verified_route_body_and_headers`; `redirect_is_refused_without_forwarding_authorization`; `response_cap_applies_to_chunked_unknown_length_body`; `request_deadline_covers_headers_and_all_response_chunks`; `operation_deadline_spans_pages_and_retains_page_one`; `upstream_statuses_and_closed_port_are_serialized_as_errors`; malformed JSON assertions in first/later-page tests | Short test deadlines and 64-byte cap use the cfg(test) loopback seam. The cap fixture sends four 32-byte chunks (128 bytes total) containing valid JSON followed by whitespace, with no Content-Length. It asserts `response_too_large`. Parameterized 401/403 and 500 cases verify error code, HTTP status, and serialized exit code; a refused local port verifies `network_error`. Production constants remain 20s request, 60s operation, 8MiB response. |
| E. Pipeline tests and checks | Tests in `src/forums.rs` and `tests/cli.rs` | `cargo test --all-targets -- --test-threads=1`: 84 library tests, 11 CLI integration tests, and example targets passed. `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, and `cargo build --release` passed. | All requested checks passed serially. |

## Explicit limits

- No live API/authenticated verification was performed in this test batch. Fixtures do not establish production availability or real credential behavior.
- Malformed first-page JSON serializes as `error` with exit code 1 and `invalid_json`; malformed later-page JSON retains prior validated rows and serializes as `partial` with exit code 3 and `invalid_json`.
- The chunked-cap fixture exercises cumulative streaming with a small cap; it does not transmit a full 8MiB payload.
- No test asserts behavior for every possible upstream pagination metadata spelling. Known continuation signals are detected and fail closed.
- All fixture accept/read paths use finite waits/timeouts and workers are joined after completion or fixture shutdown.
EOF
